    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d383">

                <pb facs="1145" n="1139" xml:id="pg1139"/>

                <head>No. 36.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Macfarlane to Mr. Blount.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic">July 13,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to your inquiry as to the rate of
                    taxation imposed upon real and personal property in the Hawaiian Kingdom
                    commencing from the reign of Kalakaua to the present time, I have the honor to
                    inform you that the rate of taxation was three-quarters of one per centum up to
                    1886, and from that time forward the rate has been 1 per centum on the assessed
                    valuation.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. C. Macfarlane.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. H. Blount</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Minister, etc.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
